From d9484acb9d3158bad78466793541023278597149 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 05:06:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Treat an owner's unknown task scope as
 unknown-not-yet with bounded wake backoff

Problem: mini's detector t_01a199d0b888e8e8 (wait-check task t_01a188a461c0178c --gateway macbook),
correctly retained on rc 3 by 2a6c4ae61b, woke at 1793939646 after three rc 2 results:
"error: replica macbook: missing successful task-scope observation for macbook/default". macbook's
gateway/info task_scopes were all {state: unknown} with no observed_at; the producer record was still in
the replica.

Why 1: kanban_wait_replica.read_task raises a generic ValueError for any non-ok matched scope, before the
StaleReplica (rc 3) classification; check() maps it to rc 2 (hermes_cli/kanban_wait_replica.py L57-59).
Why 2: kanban_wake_check counts rc 2 toward BROKEN_AFTER=3 and wakes as "broken probe"; each repark
resets the streak, so an unchanged unknown scope re-wakes every 3 probes and bypasses the offline
cooldown, which only matches stale_age results.
Why 3: a9ed7fc9ff (10-28) wrote the reader when "not ok" could only mean missing/unreadable; the
hermes-hub collector's `state: unknown` (collect_all + scope_heartbeats: a board read failing past the
450 s carry window, records kept, never tombstoned) is a well-formed "owner cannot vouch now" state
that was never given a type.
Root (happened): no typed classification for a well-formed owner-published unknown scope.
Why macbook's reads failed: UNDETERMINED (macbook unreachable; needs its hermes-hub log `collect ...
failed` lines). Not attributed.
Root (not caught): tests covered only a stale successful scope (observed_at aged) and missing scopes;
no fixture used the producer's unknown shape, and no repark test drove a non-stale unknown result.
Recurrence: second gap in the same wait path after 2a6c4ae61b (offline repark backoff).

Fix:
- read_task raises typed UnknownScope (carries the last-seen task) only for exactly one matched scope
  with state == "unknown" and no observed_at. check() returns rc 3 with `source_state=unknown
  gateway=<gw>`, no stale_age (no observation time is invented) and never `error:`. Unknown is never
  met: until/since are not evaluated. Missing, ambiguous, other states, unknown+observed_at, future
  stamps, invalid tasks and DB errors stay rc 2.
- kanban_wake_check.source_unknown() recognizes that result. It is never counted toward
  BROKEN_AFTER. First result: one typed wake (wake_check_broken reason=gateway_scope_unknown, fails=0,
  own context header). Same task/probe/gateway while a gateway_offline or gateway_scope_unknown
  receipt is under 24 h old: probe row updated, card stays scheduled. Re-escalates at most once per
  24 h. A successful scope restores normal 0/1/stale handling. The offline path shares the same
  receipt family. Dry run accepts it so the acknowledging repark is not refused;
  _remote_completed_at reads the last-seen record as it does for StaleReplica.
- recently_escalated takes a reason family (default unchanged: gateway_offline only).

Proof:
- RED on 2a6c4ae61b: 26 of 41 tests in the new/changed files fail (unknown scope -> `assert 2 == 3`).
- GREEN: 410 passed across 24 wait/wake/awaiting/remote/placement files; scripts/check ok.
- 18/18 mutants killed (each new condition, both reason-family call sites, row update, header).
- Cross-repo: real hermes-hub collect_all/stage (default read failing past the floor) -> outbox ->
  real client pull() into a reader hub.db -> core check: old core rc 2 with the incident's exact
  message; this commit rc 3 source_state=unknown; then a clean read with status done gives rc 0.
---
